(3060885, 416147, 61448, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by routerguy666:</b></div><hr/><i> I was going to say how pathetically boring this photo is, then I see it''s of Illinois so what else could it be really.  I empathize with your situation. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Pretentious:<br/>Main Entry: pre·ten·tious <br/>Pronunciation: pri-''ten(t)-sh&amp;s<br/>Function: adjective<br/>Etymology: French prétentieux, from prétention pretension, from Medieval Latin pretention-, pretentio, from Latin praetendere<br/>1 : characterized by pretension : as a : making usually unjustified or excessive claims (as of value or standing) &lt;the pretentious fraud who assumes a love of culture that is alien to him -- Richard Watts&gt; b : expressive of affected, unwarranted, or exaggerated importance, worth, or stature &lt;pretentious language&gt; &lt;pretentious houses&gt;<br/> <br/>Since your comment/attitude was pretentious... I owe you no response.</td>', 'Originally posted by routerguy666: I was going to say how pathetically boring this photo is, then I see it''s of Illinois so what else could it be really.  I empathize with your situation.   Pretentious:Main Entry: pre·ten·tious Pronunciation: pri-''ten(t)-sh&sFunction: adjectiveEtymology: French prétentieux, from prétention pretension, from Medieval Latin pretention-, pretentio, from Latin praetendere1 : characterized by pretension : as a : making usually unjustified or excessive claims (as of value or standing) <the pretentious fraud who assumes a love of culture that is alien to him -- Richard Watts> b : expressive of affected, unwarranted, or exaggerated importance, worth, or stature <pretentious language> <pretentious houses> Since your comment/attitude was pretentious... I owe you no response.', '2006-11-25 02:42:25.000000', NULL, 0),
